      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s steep hills give drivers sweeping views of downtown Denver and the Rockies from Lakewood/Dry Gulch Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_Park%2C_Denver",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Three creeks—Lakewood Gulch, Dry Gulch, and Weir Gulch—run through Villa Park, creating a riparian environment that supports bike and pedestrian paths.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_Park%2C_Denver",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The RTD W Line light rail, with stops at Knox Court, Perry Street and Sheridan Boulevard, began serving Villa Park after 2013 completion of west corridor of FasTracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_Park%2C_Denver",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 2023, the Denver City Council approved the West Area Plan, officially incorporating Villa Park into the city’s long‑term development strategy.",
